Beryllium: treat FreeBSD like Linux in Helium's added code

Purpose: Helium's patches add code with BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) conditions,
  written for Linux, Windows and macOS only. On FreeBSD that macro is false
  (GN's is_linux is true, so the Linux source files are compiled), and the
  code falls into the Windows/macOS branch. The FreeBSD port fixes the same
  problem in Chromium's own code by adding "|| BUILDFLAG(IS_BSD)"; this
  patch does the same for every IS_LINUX condition Helium adds (9
  conditions and 2 matching #endif comments, 7 files):
  - importer (brave/chrome-importer-files.patch): BSD compiles
    chrome_importer_utils_linux.cc, so it must also take the Linux branch
    of the declarations and profile list; otherwise it calls
    GetArcUserDataFolder(), which exists only on Windows and macOS. This was
    the compile error at 89% of the fourth Poudriere build (2 November 2026).
  - keyboard shortcuts (helium/core/custom-keyboard-shortcuts.patch): the
    Super key label.
  - zen mode (helium/ui/layout/zen-mode.patch): Linux desktop window
    decoration fixes, which apply to the same X11/Wayland desktop on BSD.
Stage: 4 (Beryllium series). Depends on those three Helium patches.
Refreshed against: Chromium 156.0.8078.79, Helium 0.20.3 (2f81b9ca),
  FreeBSD ports 6ad3e0c8, using freebsd/tools/patch-workbench.
Guard: freebsd/tools/helium-linux-conditions compares Helium's IS_LINUX
  conditions with the reviewed list in freebsd/helium-linux-conditions.json
  and fails CI when Helium adds or changes one.
Test: the build compiles chrome/browser/importer; functional (planned): the
  import dialog lists Linux-style browser profiles (no Arc or Canary).

